# PY184: Python 3.12+ suppresses every named APSW_FAULT injection
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (fault-injection coverage)
#
# should_fault() (tools/fi.py:942-948) requires pending_exception == (None,
# None, None). On Python 3.12+, the C side passes (None,) via PyTuple_Pack(1,
# OBJ(exc_save)) where exc_save is NULL → Py_None (faultinject.c:126-147,
# pyutil.c:17-21). (None,) != (None, None, None) is always True, so named
# faults always return False on 3.12+.
